>> If you find a bear trap in the mines

Or anywhere else in the dungeon or branches until you decide to explore
Ft Ludios.

>> and you can get to the second door
>> fast enough, apply the bear trap towards/into the doorway.  Then each
>> soldier will be trapped as they try to move throw the doorway to attack
>> you. [...]
>
> I sometimes dig a pit in front of that door, which has a similar effect.

If the doorway gets blasted then advancing monsters can move diagonally
and avoid the pit.  When the first one gets face to face with me I
figure it's time to switch from applying my poleaxe to melee.  When I've
cleared the soldiers in Ludios I've usually ended up doing melee for a
lot of them by the time it's over.

> Now that you've proposed the bear trap, it occurred to me for the first
> time that bear traps don't get triggered (as in RL), rather re-activate
> for the next victim.

It is very different from real life in that sense.


